msgid "``em`` — the module"
msgstr ""

msgid "``import em`` (or ``from s3dgraphy import em``). Generated for em API |api|."
msgstr ""

msgid "the API's own version — what a plugin's ``em_api_min``/``em_api_max`` are read against (SPEC-plugin §14.7), distinct from s3Dgraphy's and EMStudio's"
msgstr ""

msgid "Built-in immutable sequence."
msgstr ""

msgid "If no argument is given, the constructor returns an empty tuple. If iterable is specified the tuple is initialized from iterable's items."
msgstr ""

msgid "If the argument is a tuple, the return value is the same object."
msgstr ""

msgid "The host's current graph, a :class:`GraphView`; read at every access."
msgstr ""

msgid "The vocabularies, a :class:`~s3dgraphy.em.vocab.Vocab`."
msgstr ""

msgid "The packages of the document, a :class:`~s3dgraphy.em.vocab.Profiles`."
msgstr ""

msgid "Install, list, enable from disk: :class:`~s3dgraphy.em.extensions.Extensions`."
msgstr ""

msgid "What the active plugins expose to the console (``em.ext.<plugin>.<name>``)."
msgstr ""

msgid "The application half: :doc:`../context`."
msgstr ""

msgid "Functions"
msgstr ""

msgid "The command line: open an em.json in the «no application» host."
msgstr ""

msgid "The file's active graph becomes :data:`em.graph`, and the packages it declares (``header.profiles``) become :data:`em.profiles`. Inside an application the graph is the open document, so there is no ``em.open``."
msgstr ""

msgid "Parameters"
msgstr ""

msgid "an ``.em.json`` file (a container or a single graph)."
msgstr ""

msgid "Returns"
msgstr ""

msgid "the opened graph."
msgstr ""

msgid "Return type"
msgstr ""

msgid "Raises"
msgstr ""

msgid "inside an application."
msgstr ""

msgid "Example"
msgstr ""

msgid "The command line: work on a :class:`~s3dgraphy.graph.Graph` already in memory. ``author`` is the SESSION's identity (as EMStudio's editor hand): set once here, never per write."
msgstr ""

msgid "a :class:`~s3dgraphy.graph.Graph`."
msgstr ""

msgid "who is writing (an ORCID, an e-mail…). Without it (and without ``S3DGRAPHY_AUTHOR`` in the environment) every write is refused."
msgstr ""

msgid "the graph, read-only; also available as :data:`em.graph`."
msgstr ""

msgid "inside an application, where the graph is the open document."
msgstr ""

msgid "The command line: save the graph as an em.json."
msgstr ""

msgid "Writes the container the graph came from (or a new one around it) and emits ``document-saved``."
msgstr ""

msgid "where to write. Default: the file the graph was opened from."
msgstr ""

msgid "the path written."
msgstr ""

msgid "with no ``path`` when the graph did not come from a file."
msgstr ""

msgid "inside an application (the application saves)."
msgstr ""

msgid "What there is, in a few lines (and the active plugins' commands when the host has them)."
msgstr ""

msgid "Prints the summary and returns it."
msgstr ""

msgid "``\"en\"`` or ``\"it\"``; default: the host's language."
msgstr ""

msgid "the text printed."
msgstr ""

msgid "Open an act (``with em.write(\"…\") as tx:``)."
msgstr ""

msgid "Everything done on ``tx`` inside the block is applied together, as one step with one Log line, when the block ends. If the block raises, nothing is applied. The author is the session's (see :func:`em.use <s3dgraphy.em.use>`), never an argument."
msgstr ""

msgid "what the act is (shown in the Log and the undo history)."
msgstr ""

msgid "a proposal: it only adds, marked as volatile."
msgstr ""

msgid "check the act and return its delta without applying it."
msgstr ""

msgid "use it as a context manager."
msgstr ""

msgid "on leaving the block, when the contract refuses the act     (no author, a forbidden relation…). Nothing is applied."
msgstr ""

msgid "Stamp a file a plugin (or a script) made, in one line."
msgstr ""

msgid "``agent`` — the plugin (a :class:`~s3dgraphy.em.plugins.Plugin`, its ``ctx`` or ``{\"id\", \"name\", \"version\"}``); inside a plugin's command, the calling plugin when not given. ``inputs`` — paths (hashed) or identities (``{\"resource_id\": …}`` of a graph's resource, ``{\"resource_id\": …, \"kind\": \"acquisition\"}``). ``parameters``, ``dtc_kind`` (the vocabulary of ``dtc_kinds``: ``format_conversion``, ``transformation``, ``export``…), ``technique``, ``label``, ``description``, ``resource_id`` (default: derived from the digest), ``operator``, ``at``, ``tier``, ``software`` (more lines)."
msgstr ""

msgid "Writes ``<artifact>.stamp.json`` (``write=False``: only returns it) and returns the stamp. Re-stamping the same bytes writes the same record but the instant (the format: the same fact registered twice, deduplicated)."
msgstr ""

msgid "the artifact or an input path is not a file, or an input     names nothing."
msgstr ""

msgid "Subscribe ``fn(payload)`` to ``event``; usable as a decorator (``@em.on(\"graph-changed\")``). Returns a :class:`Subscription`, or ``fn`` when used as a decorator."
msgstr ""

msgid "The payload is a dict with the event's name under ``\"event\"``; for ``graph-changed`` also the step's ``label`` and the ``ids`` it touched."
msgstr ""

msgid "one of :data:`EVENTS`."
msgstr ""

msgid "the listener; omit it to use ``on`` as a decorator."
msgstr ""

msgid "an unknown event."
msgstr ""

msgid "Unsubscribe ``fn`` from ``event`` (the other way is ``Subscription.off()``)."
msgstr ""

msgid "the listener given to :func:`on`."
msgstr ""

msgid "False when ``fn`` was not subscribed."
msgstr ""

